#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "It only ever raises the number. Clearing epsilon means you can do epsilon; whether zeta is beyond you is still an open question, so if your skills already average higher, the average stands. The skill rows underneath are untouched either way, which is why they can read lower than the number above them. A course throws a mix at you, so it cannot tell you which of your skills got you through it."
