#~ msgid "The reason is the osu! API. The site notices you are playing through osu!'s feed of new scores, and that feed only lists scores on charts with a leaderboard, so a play on a graveyarded chart never shows up in it. Your recent plays are a separate lookup that does include graveyarded charts, but it has to be asked per player, so the site only starts asking once a leaderboard score shows you are playing, and keeps asking every few minutes until you stop. Everything it finds during that time counts, including unranked charts. <0>If you only play unranked charts, nothing is recorded until you set a score on a chart with a leaderboard.</0>"
