#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "The site does not use the accuracy the game showed you. It works it out again from your judgements, the 300s, 200s, 100s and so on. Mania has two ways of adding those up, the stable formula and the ScoreV2 one that lazer shows, and each ladder writes its bar in one of them: 4K regular in stable, 4K LN in ScoreV2. Since the two print different numbers for the same play, recomputing is what makes that play count, or not count, the same on either client."
#~ msgstr "The site does not use the accuracy the game showed you. It works it out again from your judgements, the 300s, 200s, 100s and so on. Mania has two ways of adding those up, the stable formula and the ScoreV2 one that lazer shows, and each ladder writes its bar in one of them: 4K regular in stable, 4K LN in ScoreV2. Since the two print different numbers for the same play, recomputing is what makes that play count, or not count, the same on either client."

