msgid "Your accuracy sets the tier. On a ladder whose courses ask for 96%, a bare 96% pass on the delta course reads as <0>delta</0>, 97.5% as <1>delta+</1>, and 98% and up as <2>delta++</2>. Come up short and you still get something for it: 95% reads as <3>delta-</3> and 94% as <4>delta--</4>. Below 94% you get nothing. Ladders that ask for a different accuracy shift the whole scale with them."
msgstr "Your accuracy sets the tier. On a ladder whose courses ask for 96%, a bare 96% pass on the delta course reads as <0>delta</0>, 97.5% as <1>delta+</1>, and 98% and up as <2>delta++</2>. Come up short and you still get something for it: 95% reads as <3>delta-</3> and 94% as <4>delta--</4>. Below 94% you get nothing. Ladders that ask for a different accuracy shift the whole scale with them."

