#~ msgstr "Your accuracy sets the tier. On a ladder whose courses ask for 96%, a bare 96% pass on the delta course reads as <0>delta</0>, 97.5% as <1>delta+</1>, and 98% and up as <2>delta++</2>. Come up short at 94% and you still get <3>delta--</3>, since getting that close is worth something. Below that you get nothing. Ladders that ask for a different accuracy shift the whole scale with them."

